# speaking — a Speaking modus mentis puts conversation first
#
# Observing: Banter (Observation + Speaking) is handed the crate in the Test Hall. The crate is kept
# (the playground never turns away), and the follow-up observation is narrowed to the one living
# person still unobserved, the brewer, out of every object left in the hall. The line turning
# to him ("shifts to the brewer") is what proves he was the one attended to.
#
# Thinking: Rhetoric (Thinking + Speaking), thinking about the brewer, is offered only the
# conversations among his goals, and a conversation's means are narrowed to the one speaking
# action modus mentis held, Boasting — so the button reads "[Boasting …]" and offers no attack.
#
# Not reachable here: a speaking action modus mentis never refusing a conversation (the playground
# always answers "willing"), and never turning away from a person (the playground never turns away,
# and --refuse-focus deliberately wins over the rule).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Hall" --period dawn --grant-mm banter,rhetoric,boasting,knack

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180

# Banter observes the crate, then turns to the brewer rather than to another object.
click keyword crate
choose 1
choose banter
advance 12 180
expect shifts to the brewer

# Rhetoric thinks about the brewer: a conversation, carried out by Boasting.
strategy succeed
click keyword man
choose 0
choose rhetoric
advance 12 180
expect [Boasting
expect-not attack him
expect-not [Knack
quit
